- accept
	join Ardana(d) left
	join Marius(flustered) right
	Ardana: thank you…
- decline
	join Ardana(d) left
	join Marius(flustered) right
	Ardana: I’m good.
Marius: I just thought because you know.
Marius: People said tea calms the mind.
Marius: That’s all!
Marius: ....
Ardana(confused): okay?
Marius(d): ...
Marius: ahem
Marius: I added more herbs to help you sleep.
Marius: I saw how bothered you looked…
Marius: Maybe this will calm your mind, even a little.
Ardana: ...
Ardana(smile): How thoughtful.
[i]You remember the times your mother used to bring you tea when times were tough
Ardana(d): ...
- Continue the conversation
	Ardana: You're unusually talkative right now.
	Marius(rattled): ...
	Marius(d): Ahem.
	Marius: I am but your humble servant, your highness.
	Marius: I obey your will without question.
	Marius: For my sword and life is yours.
	Ardana(confused): hm...
	Ardana(d): Your duty is to God.
	Ardana: Is it not?
	Ardana: If there was a choice between me and heaven.
	Ardana(melancholy): What would happen then?
	Marius(concerned): ...
	Marius: My duty is to help you spread the gospel, your highness.
	Marius: It is written in the passages that you are to be our destined ruler.
	Marius(empathetic): Isn't that part of my duty then?
	Ardana(rattled): ...
	Ardana: I suppose you're right
	chuckle
	Ardana(smile): You really did calm me down.
	
- Wish him goodnight
	Ardana(d): I'm quite tired, thank you for the gesture.
Ardana(d): Good night sir Marius.
Marius(d): Good night, your highness.
leave --All--